    "result_text": "The full suite ran green (`Tests run: 1, Failures: 0, Errors: 0`). Done.\n\n## Summary\n\nI implemented the `GOLD` membership tier rule: `membershipTier` becomes `'GOLD'` when an owner's household (owners sharing the same `householdId`) has 3+ members, otherwise the existing SILVER/BRONZE rules apply.\n\nThe tier is a **derived field** computed by `OwnerMapper` at response time from a single `Owner`, so the challenge was getting household size to the mapper. Since the test DB uses `ddl-auto=none` (schema fixed by `schema.sql`), I avoided a schema change by using a transient field.\n\nChanges:\n- **`Owner.java`** \u2014 added a `@Transient` `householdMemberCount` field (not persisted) with accessors.\n- **`util/MembershipTiers.java`** (new) \u2014 `tierFor(Owner)`: returns `GOLD` when `householdMemberCount >= 3`, else the prior SILVER/BRONZE logic.\n- **`OwnerMapper.java`** \u2014 the `membershipTier` mapping expression now delegates to `MembershipTiers.tierFor(owner)`.\n- **`HouseholdMembers.java`** (new) \u2014 counts/stamps live household size (owners sharing a non-blank `householdId`; a null/blank id is a household of one) from the currently-stored owners.\n- **Responder/list functions** (`RespondWithOwner`, `RespondWithOwnerCreated`, `RespondWithOwnerUpdated`, `ListOwners`, `ListOwnersPage`) \u2014 stamp the count before mapping, so GET/create/update/list all report the tier consistently. No YAML changes were needed (`OwnerRepository` injects by type into the functions).\n- **`openapi.yml`** \u2014 updated the `membershipTier` description to document the GOLD rule.\n\nBecause the count is computed live from stored owners (the new owner is already saved by response time, and `AssignHousehold` back-fills the shared `householdId` onto existing members), the third household member correctly reports `GOLD` on GET.",
